.TH ROOT-GIT-CONFIGURATION 7 "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
root-git-configuration \- headless root Git, private machine settings and etckeeper backup
.SH DESCRIPTION
The public dotfiles repository renders /root/.gitconfig with noninteractive
credential defaults and a hostname-specific include at
/etc/gitconfig.d/<hostname>.conf. The include may initially be absent.
No desktop Secret Service, graphical OAuth, or personal user credentials are
needed for etckeeper. Ordinary users retain their existing Git configuration.
.PP
The private arrans-private-overlay checkout is the source for non-secret,
machine-specific Git and SSH configuration. It is not itself an authentication
secret store. Root's chezmoi run_after_deploy-private-root-git.sh script
copies matching files into their installed locations, but does not rewrite
/etc/.git/config or replace the stock etckeeper hooks.
.SH FILE OWNERSHIP
.TP
Public Git (version controlled, continuously managed)
home/dot_gitconfig.tmpl renders /root/.gitconfig.
home/private_dot_ssh/private_config.tmpl renders /root/.ssh/config.
.TP
Public Git (version controlled, create-only)
home/create_dot_gitconfig.local.tmpl initially creates
/root/.gitconfig.local, preserving any subsequent changes.
.TP
Private Git (version controlled, continuously installed)
config/git/<hostname>.conf becomes /etc/gitconfig.d/<hostname>.conf.
config/git/<hostname>.etckeeper.conf becomes
/etc/gitconfig.d/<hostname>.etckeeper.conf.
config/ssh/<hostname>.conf becomes /root/.ssh/config.d/<hostname>.conf.
A new root chezmoi application is required after private-overlay updates.
.TP
Machine-local (optionally generated, not version controlled)
The private SSH identity /root/.ssh/etckeeper_gitlab and its public key
are generated only when an SSH host snippet is present and neither file
already exists. Existing or incomplete pairs are never overwritten.
.TP
Existing local Git metadata
/etc/.git/config remains owned by etckeeper/Git. Git's includeIf rule
supplies a push URL only for the /etc repository, without changing the
remote's stored fetch URL.
.SH SETUP
.SS 1. Apply public dotfiles to root
Ensure chezmoi is installed for root, and apply your existing arran4/dotfiles
source with root's HOME set to /root. Do not copy the desktop user's
chezmoi state into root. Example after root has been initialised:
.PP
.nf
sudo -H chezmoi apply
.fi
.SS 2. Sync private overlay
.PP
.nf
sudo emaint sync -r arrans-private-overlay
sudo -H chezmoi apply
.fi
.PP
The second apply installs /etc/gitconfig.d/<hostname>.conf, any
etckeeper-specific include, and the root SSH host snippet. It may create
/root/.ssh/etckeeper_gitlab if absent. It never recreates an existing key.
Only hosts with a matching source file are changed.
.SS 3. Authorise the machine's public key
.PP
.nf
sudo cat /root/.ssh/etckeeper_gitlab.pub
.fi
.PP
Add the PUBLIC key to the corresponding private GitLab etckeeper project's
Settings > Repository > Deploy keys and grant write access. Use one key
per machine. No plaintext key material goes in either Git repository.
GitLab authorisation is an external security boundary and is not faked
or bypassed during bootstrap.
.SS 4. Verify the SSH server host key
StrictHostKeyChecking remains enabled. Obtain the GitLab server's SSH
host-key fingerprint from a trusted administrator or an out-of-band
source. Compare it with the key returned by ssh-keyscan before authorising
the key. Once independently verified, run the explicit first-connection
SSH bootstrap (a one-time trust prompt writes root's known_hosts):
.PP
.nf
sudo -H ssh -o StrictHostKeyChecking=ask -T gitlab-arran-etckeeper
.fi
.PP
Accept the prompt only if the presented fingerprint matches the trusted
fingerprint. A permission-denied response can still mean the host key was
recorded; ensure the deploy key is authorised separately. Do not silently
trust an unauthenticated scan or disable strict checking for normal pushes.
.SS 5. Verify effective configuration
.PP
.nf
sudo -H git config --global --show-origin --get-all credential.helper
sudo -H git config --global --get credential.interactive
sudo -H git -C /etc config --show-origin --get-regexp '^remote\..*\.pushurl$'
sudo -H git -C /etc remote get-url --push origin
sudo -H git -C /etc status --short
sudo -H env GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 git -C /etc push origin
.fi
.PP
The push URL should use the dedicated GitLab SSH host alias. Check the
actual remote name and branch before issuing a push on machines with
different etckeeper settings. The push remains immediate and synchronous.
.SS 6. Keep etckeeper pushing
.PP
The stock Portage etckeeper hooks continue to commit and, if enabled by
PUSH_REMOTE, push changes at their normal trigger points. Confirm
/etc/etckeeper/etckeeper.conf retains an appropriate PUSH_REMOTE setting.
This integration does not install a service, timer or replacement hook.
.SH SECURITY
/etc is version-tracked by etckeeper and may be pushed to a backup server.
Therefore /etc/gitconfig.d must contain only non-secret configuration.
Public dotfiles and private-overlay Git history must never contain
plaintext tokens, passwords or SSH private keys. Chezmoi-managed
configuration may be overwritten during subsequent applies; create-only
and generated local credentials are intentionally not.
.PP
The private overlay checkout is a deployment dependency, not a runtime
dependency. Missing source files do not remove already-installed settings.
Invalid source files stop installation before replacement. A required
credential or verified SSH host key that has not yet been provisioned
causes the normal push to fail noninteractively.
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
Use ssh -G gitlab-arran-etckeeper to inspect root's effective SSH
configuration without connecting; check that identity and host-key
verification are correct. Use git config --show-origin to identify
unexpected credential helpers and rewrite rules. Never paste private
keys or tokens into issue reports.
.SH SEE ALSO
chezmoi(1), git-config(1), ssh_config(5), etckeeper(8), dispatch-conf(1)
